<section class="shell-summary" aria-labelledby="tech-h"><h2 id="tech-h">How this site works</h2>
<ul>
<li>It is generated at build time from the library's <code>policy.yml</code> manifests: {{summary.found}} found, {{summary.valid}} valid{{#summary.invalid}}, {{summary.invalid}} invalid{{/summary.invalid}}. Built {{summary.builtAt}}{{#summary.sourceCommit}} from commit <code>{{summary.sourceCommit}}</code>{{/summary.sourceCommit}}.</li>
<li>The data is a SQLite database. It runs in your browser with sql.js (WebAssembly); there is no server and nothing you type is sent anywhere.</li>
<li>Queries run locally, read-only, against the downloadable <code>library.sqlite</code>.</li>
</ul></section>
<p class="note"><strong>file:// limitation:</strong> the search below fetches <code>library.sqlite</code> and loads WebAssembly, which browsers block when the page is opened straight from disk. It works over http (GitHub Pages, or a local web server). The catalog and policy pages do not need it.</p>
